README.md
Execution Gateway (EG) — Minimal Reference (Go 1.22, Ed25519)

What this is
- A compact, runnable “Execution Gateway” that:
  - Mints capability-scoped intent tokens (CIT) with Ed25519 (demo)
  - Verifies CITs and executes structured requests
  - Applies simple policy/risk checks (first-time payee, after-hours, urgent language)
  - Logs signed receipts to an append-only JSONL file
  - Accepts AI-to-AI attestations and assigns basic trust tiers
  - Supports revoking JTIs and freezing compartments

Prereqs
- Go 1.22+
- jq (for scripts)
- curl

Quick start (local)
- make build
- ./bin/eg
- In a second terminal, run demos:

1) Attestation (establish a verified counterparty)
- ./scripts/demo_attest.sh

2) Happy path: $150 to known payee (pre-verified; under cap)
- ./scripts/demo_happy.sh
  - Expect status=allowed with signed receipt

3) Deny: first-time payee, urgent language, over cap
- ./scripts/demo_deny.sh
  - Expect status=deny with next_step.live_confirm

4) Block: non-delegable action
- ./scripts/demo_block.sh
  - Expect status=block

Logs
- Decisions append to eg-decisions.log as JSONL.
- Receipts include base64 Ed25519 signatures over the receipt JSON (demo).

Environment variables
- EG_ED25519_PRIV_HEX: optional hex private key for CIT verification (demo). If absent, generated at boot.
- EG_RECEIPT_PRIV_HEX: optional hex private key for receipt signing.

Notes and limitations (demo)
- CIT is a compact Ed25519-signed payload minted by /mint_cit for demo. In production: mint only on trusted user devices and keep chat models unable to mint.
- /attest is a stub (no mTLS); tiering is heuristic for demo purposes.
- No persistence beyond append-only log; JTI cache is in-memory (Redis can be added).
- Risk engine minimal; no real per-day ledger/caps tracking here.

Docker
- make docker
- docker run -p 8080:8080 eg:dev

Extending
- Add Redis for JTI cache and a real policy store.
- Replace stub attestation with mTLS + signed headers.
- Implement COSE_Sign1 receipts and JOSE/COSE interop.
- Add policy-change governor, shadow-mode, and non-delegable registry.

